WEBVTT

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:04.640
Three.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.680
Two.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.310
One.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.010
Zero!

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.390
I prayed it wouldn't come to this.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.920
You're making a choice for the sake of the mission.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.520
It isn't a choice.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.610
We have no choice.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.110
I'm against it!

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.140
Totally against it!

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.070
Sue!

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.930
He's already escaped from the base twice.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.280
How can you just fence him in?

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.280
We have no idea how he'll react!

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:50.650
Plus...

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.190
Using Harriet is the problem.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.150
Isn't it?

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.620
Yes, it is.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.490
It was the trauma she felt
that made him break out.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.280
But what made her decide to return here?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.700
What did happen, Lt. Soma?

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.000
She understood.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.500
She realized this was
the only place she had left.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.270
However, even if she decides to help us...

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.410
...nothing guarantees the EX-1
will continue to listen to her.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.090
The risk is too great.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.380
We have...

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.200
...a contingency plan.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.590
A good luck charm?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.660
That's right.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.650
To protect Mr. Fairy.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.600
So nothing like what happened
to Walton will happen to him.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.630
Understand?

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.310
Y-Yeah.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.340
I'll go talk to him!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.440
Good girl.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.180
Mr. Fairy, that's a good luck charm!

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.510
Don't move!

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.900
It looks more like a mask than a collar.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.410
Like Phantom of the Opera, no...

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.610
Frankenstein's monster is more like it.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.950
A tapestry of parts woven from other aliens.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.090
Frank.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.820
The EX-1's creator called him that.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.680
Dr. Noguchi's report, right?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.630
We may just find the answer
the old man was looking for.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:20.600
Answer?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.970
That face guard does more than track him.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.970
It also measures
the electronic pulse of his brain.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.580
So if we can analyze that data...

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.510
We may solve all of the mysteries.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.280
What the aliens are. Where they're from.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.480
And...

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.210
Why they head for the Pilgrimage Point.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.500
Long-range radar detected an object...

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.800
...heading for Earth
at high speeds in region 38.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.400
It's an alien.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.400
Engaging intercept system.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.070
Target entering barosphere.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:06.850
Missed.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.430
Missile off mark.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.780
And the lasers?

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.450
Unable to fire.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.480
The Earth right now is like
a tennis racket without strings.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.360
Target now entering atmosphere.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.600
Expected to touch ground at E015, S030.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.460
That's inside the yellow zone!

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.590
Commander...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.420
SARG 1, SARG 3, stand by.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.420
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.660
Lieutenants Harris and Soma, remain at HQ.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:52.450
Captain.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.130
Ma'am!

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.090
Move out!

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:40.570
I don't want to go against
the commander's plan...

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:44.910
...but I'm not too thrilled about
what that alien tapestry might do.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:47.580
Let the rookies keep the bench warm.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.020
Formation Charlie!

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:51.980
Roger!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:14.650
Fire!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.390
It went right through!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.080
This thing's...

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.810
...a progressive alien!

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.200
They can't make a dent.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.100
When the solid is hurt,
the liquid takes over.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.550
It's part liquid.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:45.270
Hurry up with that data!

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:49.710
We have nothing on it
or similar aliens in our database.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.900
That's a problem.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.610
I am designating the target as type M-1.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.910
Can the EX-1 be deployed?

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.810
Face guard and neck bolt prepared.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.690
Ready.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.510
You're not getting to the red zone!

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.250
Firing liquid at maximum!

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.310
Slug mode. Fire!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.490
It's a zombie!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.720
Guenevere, can you move?

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:45.390
My machinery's okay...

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:48.460
...but I don't think I can take any more.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:52.930
Those engineers didn't think
much about the pilots...

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.170
Dan! Guenevere!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.690
Return to base!

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:58.460
Damn, going with the dark horse.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.370
This is Mistel.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:05.510
We've confirmed Harriet's
heart rate and brain pulse...

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.850
...are being transmitted to the EX-1.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.950
Roger, HQ is too.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.540
These weird clothes don't feel good.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.160
I don't see why they have to do all this.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.390
We know the EX-1
responds to Harriet's voice.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:26.470
But it could also be something else
we're not aware of.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:28.890
We have to rule out other possibilities.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:35.280
Well, better than using a SARG
to drop him in front of an enemy.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:42.570
Harriet, can you ask Mr. Fairy
to take care of the bad guy?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:45.910
Hurry.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:47.950
Okay.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.850
Mr. Fairy!

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.900
You can do it, Mr. Fairy!

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.950
You did it!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.600
You did it, Mr. Fairy!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.040
The bad guy came back!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.350
The EX-1 can't beat it...

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.390
Mr. Fairy!

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.820
Commander.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.930
There's only one alternative.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.480
Call the military!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.110
Nuclear is the only solution.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.400
Captain.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.740
Yes, ma'am?

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:45.870
It's too early to switch pitchers.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.140
Yes, ma'am...

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:50.230
We have to give him
more time on the mound.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.250
But...

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.010
It's near the red zone.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:55.540
We have to do something now.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.250
We'll use this.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:03.240
You don't care about losing the EX-1?

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.620
Losing the EX-1?

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:09.360
W-What's that mean?

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:10.450
Captain!

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.240
It's confidential.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.710
I shouldn't tell you this, but...

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:44.600
There's a thermonuclear reactor
attached to the EX-1's neck bolt.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.970
It's a contingency plan, our insurance...

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:52.270
If we lose control, we can always blow him up.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:53.400
No way!

00:14:56.680 --> 00:15:02.740
It's detonated if signals here
and at HQ are sent simultaneously.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.180
That's horrible! Horrible!

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.380
If you do it...

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.350
Mr. Fairy!

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.410
What would happen to Hattie?

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:20.210
But if we use it, it'll stop the alien
from entering the red zone.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.760
The EX-1 is a superior weapon.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.760
A weapon has to be usable.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.770
So making a martyr of him sounds fine to me.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:41.080
Lt. Soma expressed my thoughts as well.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.750
This is to avert a crisis.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.120
Commander...

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:49.160
...is what you want to protect world peace,

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.200
or your position at Funeral?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.700
We can debate this after it's over.

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.800
You can do it, Mr. Fairy!

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:09.040
What is it, Sue?

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.020
I can't see!

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:12.730
Three.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:14.790
Two.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:16.690
One.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:18.520
Zero!

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.040
Mr. Fairy!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:41.880
Captain, what happened?

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:48.190
The reactor we put on the EX-1
is higher than a class 10.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:52.490
If we detonated it here,
we'd get the residential area.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:56.200
The residents were evacuated into shelters.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.060
It's no concern.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:59.590
But Universal University's there!

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:08.470
<i>Where springs become summers,
and green meadows lie.</i>

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:14.340
<i>And the babbling brooks babble,
and the dragonflies fly.</i>

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:19.670
That's an old song.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.200
Mr. Fairy!

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.960
He's in trouble!

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.240
Somebody...

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.110
Somebody help him!

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.880
If we lose the university facility...

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.650
...it would impact
the national space program!

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:31.160
Captain.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.260
What is it?

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:34.460
I have an idea.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.620
If we stop its regeneration,
we can destroy its brain.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.070
You know how to do that?

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:58.220
There might be something at
Universal University's rocket lab.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:18.600
Do you know someone
at the university?

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:19.940
No.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:23.140
You seem to know a lot
about their facilities.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.480
There it is.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.650
Liquid oxygen?

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.510
It's used for rocket fuel.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:48.300
No more!

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.140
No more, Mr. Fairy!

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.800
Leave him alone!

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.460
Let's go home!

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.540
Not yet!

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:01.380
Lt. Harris!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.350
Here goes.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.330
Do it!

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.240
Hooray!

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:51.890
HQ, get the recovery crew in quickly.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.010
It'd be a problem if this thing came back.

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:02.940
Thanks to Lt. Soma,
we still have the EX-1, but...

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.840
...you must be disciplined.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.970
Yes, ma'am. Do as you will.

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:10.740
You're a brave man, aren't you.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:13.450
Enough. Dismissed.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:14.490
Ma'am?

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.220
Didn't you hear me?

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.190
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:25.490
Good job, Mr. Fairy!

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.380
Ta-da!

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:42.970
This is your reward!

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:00.270
Don't I draw well?

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:02.260
Does it make you happy?

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:10.210
Boo!

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:17.480
Are you a hero?

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:20.250
Or a villain?

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:26.910
I'm Ryu Soma.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:35.080
Escape and Memories

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:39.640
All you can do in a sky of memories is fly.

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.340
Flapping your wings.

00:22:41.940 --> 00:22:44.640
A couple, like canaries in a cage...

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:48.750
Next time,
Memories and Loneliness.
